{"kind":"event","event_id":9585,"event_uid":"01M2Q6JH2W9Z9D6CXTDX8GT0RV","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":399,"issue_uid":"01M2Q6F2WGQTVK5PW8VZ5CGBSZ","issue_short_id":"gbsz","actor":"impl:2@run-181","hlc_physical_ms":1789632529500,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"376984e3106bede83751fac7a87ecc179316eff8fd364b93aefdb8f14452c416","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2Q6JH2W9Z9D6CXTDW933AZ5","author":"impl:2@run-181","body":"Task 2 approach: three edits in fleet/CONTRACT.md (evidence listing's residuals.jsonl sentence gains the jev object and a residuals-jev.jsonl sentence before kata.jsonl; the Publish bullet gains the 'Act on these' clause between the table sentence and the Residuals sentence, the opening sentence's reviewer's-sentence phrase gains the errands/Act-on-these exception, and the later above-the-record sentence is rewritten to admit the rows and drop 'at all') and one in fleet/RUNBOOK.md (a **TypeSafe.** Traps label with exactly two rows between **The Claude proxy.** and **The GitHub edge.**, taking the Traps row count from 40 to 42). Documents only; no script, no role file.","created_at":"2026-09-17T08:08:49.500022602Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T08:08:49.5Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":9590,"event_uid":"01M2Q6MG9WNZ8ET9XWCD2V0W60","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":398,"issue_uid":"01M2Q6EZHKF45451GPS00YDHSH","issue_short_id":"dhsh","actor":"exam:1@run-181","hlc_physical_ms":1789632594236,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"1dab6a6fa82b4458753c293f0653a5e437a3ea3581ca02676fee74012c711b58","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2Q6MG9VYE00NTT9CEN27T5W","author":"exam:1@run-181","body":"examiner: writing the exam for task 1 (the card's `Act on these` section) into fleet/tests/test_sandbox_boot_residuals.mjs, under a comment naming this task, beside run-178's six legs.\n\nThe approach, leg by leg:\n\n- THE FIXTURE is the Context's: the rig's `DEFAULT_REPORT` with a fourteen-piece `notes` on its one done task (`p01 …` through `p14 …`, joined by `; `), the rig's default `{\"verdict\":\"PASS\"}` receipt (no ack), so the checklist is fourteen `task 1 reviewer` items and nothing else. The existing `bootOnce(tag, env, prepare)` is reused with `STUB_REPORT`/`STUB_GATE_RECEIPT` overridden in `env` — its spread puts the case's env after the file's own three-item fixture.\n- FIVE new boots, all started eagerly beside the file's existing four: `fourteen` (a `STUB_TYPESAFE_ANSWERS` file mapping needle `pNN` to the score the Context pins), `onlyP05` (p05 at 2.5, every other piece 1.0), `exit7` (`STUB_TYPESAFE_EXIT=7` over the same fixture), `allLow` (every piece 2.4), and `rigDefault` (the rig's own report and receipt, the default reply at 0.8).\n- (a) [M1] the fourteen boot's body: the line after the table's last `| … |` row is blank, the next is exactly `Act on these: 11 of 14`, then blank, then exactly ten consecutive `- ` lines string-equal to the entries for p04 p01 p07 p14 p06 p13 p05 p12 p02 p10 at 3.0 2.9 2.8 2.8 2.7 2.7 2.6 2.6 2.5 2.5, then blank, then `Residuals: 14 from review`; p11/p03/p08/p09's texts absent from every line above that; and `onlyP05` renders `Act on these: 1 of 14` with p05's single entry at `attention 2.5`.\n- (b) [M2] `rigDefault`, `exit7` and `allLow` each carry no line beginning `Act on these`.\n- (c) [M3] the fourteen boot's body with its `Act on these`-to-`Residuals:` span spliced out is string-equal to `exit7`'s; both carry `Residuals: 14 from review`, `Amendments: none` and fourteen `- [ ] task 1 reviewer — ` lines under `### Residuals` in checklist order; same `mergePuts` length; the fourteen boot's `typesafe.log` holds exactly fourteen lines.\n\nThe one sub-clause the exam cannot encode is leg (c)'s last: \"the first `Run:` runs the card-cells sim green on the edited script\". `test_sims_are_hermetic.mjs` M4 forbids a sim from spawning another sim, so that reading stays the driver's `Run:` line, named in the file header and returned under `unsatisfiable`. Nothing else in the Proof is left out.","created_at":"2026-09-17T08:09:54.235369844Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T08:09:54.236Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":9596,"event_uid":"01M2Q6MQ8XKAW47A0SGXB5M0ZN","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":398,"issue_uid":"01M2Q6EZHKF45451GPS00YDHSH","issue_short_id":"dhsh","actor":"impl:1@run-181","hlc_physical_ms":1789632601373,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"31ee3b260c358c55ec0f94cc86f7793b6cf116734d7d661f9a70e4a8721fac3e","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2Q6MQ8W53MPG2FBM165QP4K","author":"impl:1@run-181","body":"Approach for task 1 (the card's `Act on these` section).\n\nSite: `card_head` (fleet/sandbox-boot.sh ~2787) is one single-quoted `python3 -c` program. The section goes between the task table loop and the `Residuals:` line built at ~3003, appended as `[\"\", \"Act on these: <q> of <n>\", \"\"] + entries` so the existing `out += [\"\", \"Residuals: ...\"]` supplies the trailing blank — which makes M3's splice (from the `Act on these` line up to, not including, the `Residuals:` line) yield exactly the no-section body.\n\nRows: `render_card` already reads `residuals=\"$(residual_items || true)\"`; it will also read `rows=\"$(residual_rows || true)\"` and pass it to `card_head` as a THIRD ARGV STRING (the Context allows argument, file or second stdin document). No new file, no new request — `rows` mode never calls `fleet_curl`, it reads the cache `residual_jev` filled inside `collect_evidence`.\n\nZip by index: `checklist` and `rows` modes are two calls of the same `residual_read` walk over the same two documents, so the nth row is the nth checklist item. The entry takes its `<name> — <text>` off the checklist item verbatim and its attention/actor/status/subject off the row's `jev`; a row whose request failed has no `jev` key and is not a candidate.\n\nThreshold 2.5 inclusive, `\"%.1f\"`, sort by -attention (stable, so ties keep checklist order), cap at ten, and no section at all when no row qualifies. Nothing gates on it.","created_at":"2026-09-17T08:10:01.372452309Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T08:10:01.373Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":9607,"event_uid":"01M2Q6NN0WBPSV0GCJ2WX5NQK4","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":399,"issue_uid":"01M2Q6F2WGQTVK5PW8VZ5CGBSZ","issue_short_id":"gbsz","actor":"impl:2@run-181","hlc_physical_ms":1789632631836,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"d23c2c2c01f64e9d86779f63fba82775a97320a758d51b809d87eb4c55fc8f21","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2Q6NN0VZZXEK16PBGSSHYTJ","author":"impl:2@run-181","body":"Done: all 11 proof lines green on HEAD (58ea2bb3); footprint is fleet/CONTRACT.md and fleet/RUNBOOK.md only (+38/-6). Two decisions worth recording: (1) the evidence listing states the jev key order in prose rather than as a JSON literal, because the row's keys are sorted (actor, attention, claim_false, confidence, kind, model) while M1's ordering asks for kind.status/kind.subject first — the sorted-key fact is stated on the residuals.jsonl key list instead; (2) the RUNBOOK's TypeSafe rows name TYPESAFE_API_KEY only to say no such key is on any VM's disk or argv — the name, never a value, which is what M4 pins and what the no-credential constraint allows. test_sandbox_boot_card_cells.mjs and test_sandbox_boot_amendments.mjs, the two sims that read the Publish bullet, still pass.","created_at":"2026-09-17T08:10:31.835428913Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T08:10:31.836Z"}
